cimal places. We'll use round(gain / prediction_tokens, 6). Also need to ensure we don't mutate case. We'll iterate over calls.\n\nOutput must be JSON with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics. diagnostics array in same order as calls.\n\nWe'll produce Python code that defines solve(case) returning dict.\n\nWe must also abide by the explicit case interface: solve(case) gets the payload directly, not the outer case_id etc. So case is the payload object.\n\nWe'll implement:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case['threshold']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    accepted = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        norm_gain = round((call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']) / call['prediction_tokens'], 6)\n        accepted_flag = call['parseable'] and norm_gain >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            'accepted': accepted_flag,\n            'call_id': call['call_id'],\n            'normalized_gain': norm_gain\n        })\n        if accepted_flag:\n            accepted.append(call['call_id'])\n    return {'accepted_call_ids': accepted, 'diagnostics': diagnostics}\n\nThat seems straightforward.\n\nNow we need to output JSON string with key \"implementation\" and value being the Python source code as a JSON string. Escape properly.\n\nWe must ensure the code uses only standard library. It does.\n\nLet's produce the final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2087,"completion_tokens":723,"total_tokens":2810,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":543},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":39},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}